# Copy to .env and fill in. No real values belong in this file.

# Postgres connection string (Neon). Used by Prisma and the engineering-data routes.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require

# --- Enquiry email via n8n (lib/notify.ts) --- OPTIONAL ---
# Every enquiry from /purchase, the Get a Quote modal and the valve inquiry
# forms is saved to the database and listed at /admin/enquiries. That row is
# the record, so an enquiry is never lost when this is unset.
# Setting it adds an email notification on top; leaving it unset means
# someone must watch /admin/enquiries instead.

# Production URL of the n8n Webhook node that sends the email. The site POSTs
# { "subject": "...", "text": "..." }; the workflow owns sender and recipients.
ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Only if the Webhook node uses Header Auth: sent as "Authorization: Bearer <token>".
ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=

# --- Razorpay (lib/razorpay.ts) --- needed for "Pay" on /cost ---
# Key pair from Dashboard > Settings > API Keys. Test keys (rzp_test_...) for
# staging, live keys only in the Production environment.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
# Dashboard > Settings > Webhooks > add https://www.gmdalui.co.in/api/razorpay/webhook
# with event "payment.captured"; the secret you type there goes here.
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- Deployment runbook ---
#
# 0. REQUIRED, before the first deploy: apply pending database migrations, or
#    every enquiry form returns an error because the table does not exist.
#       npx prisma migrate deploy
#    Enquiries then appear at /admin/enquiries (sign in as ADMIN or DEVELOPER).
#    This is the only step that must happen for enquiries to work. Steps 1-6
#    are only needed if you also want an email for each one.
#
# 1. In n8n, build a workflow: Webhook node (POST, Respond: Immediately) ->
#    email node (Gmail / SMTP / etc.) with Subject = {{ $json.body.subject }}
#    and Text = {{ $json.body.text }}. Set the recipient(s) on the email node.
#    Activate the workflow and copy the Webhook node's PRODUCTION URL (the test
#    URL only works while the editor's "Listen for test event" is running).
# 2. If you enabled Header Auth on the Webhook node, use header name
#    "Authorization" and value "Bearer <token>"; that token is ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_TOKEN.
# 3. In the hosting dashboard (Vercel) > the project > Settings > Environment
#    Variables, add for the Production environment:
#       ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL   = the production webhook URL
#       ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_TOKEN = the token from step 2 (omit if no auth)
# 4. Redeploy. Environment variables are only picked up by a NEW deployment -
#    saving them changes nothing until you redeploy.
# 5. Confirm: open https://www.gmdalui.co.in/api/health in a browser.
#       "mail":"configured"      -> ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL is present. Go to step 6.
#       "mail":"not-configured"  -> it is missing or you did not redeploy.
# 6. "configured" only means the URL exists, not that mail leaves the building.
#    Send ONE real enquiry through the Get a Quote form on the live site and
#    check it lands in the inbox (also spam). If not, open the workflow's
#    Executions tab in n8n: no execution = wrong URL or workflow not active;
#    a failed execution = the email node's credentials.
#    Cross-check against /admin/enquiries: a row there with "Not emailed" is an
#    enquiry that reached us but that nobody was notified about.
#
# --- Secrets ---
# Never commit a real .env. One was committed to this repo before (a Razorpay
# test-mode key pair, in src/components/.env) and the repo is public, so that
# pair must be treated as compromised and rotated. Payment keys belong only in
# the hosting dashboard's environment variables, never in NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars,
# which are compiled into the browser bundle.

# Shared secret gmd-quotation sends as x-api-key to POST /api/lookup-options/sync.
LOOKUP_SYNC_API_KEY=
